# Line-ending policy for files whose bytes matter outside Git.
#
# `scripts/ci/assert-image.sh` runs under `sh` inside the image and on Linux CI
# runners. A CRLF checkout turns its shebang into `#!/bin/sh\r`, which fails with
# "bad interpreter: No such file or directory" — and it fails only in CI, because
# nothing on a Windows host ever executes the file. `core.autocrlf=true` (the
# Windows default) does exactly that on checkout, so these paths are pinned.
#
# The Dockerfile is pinned for the same class of reason: a trailing `\r` after a
# line-continuation `\` turns the next line into an argument instead of a command.
# Docker tolerates CRLF in some paths, but relying on that tolerance is not a plan.
#
# Deliberately narrow: a global `* text=auto` would renormalise every file in the
# repository and bury this rule in a whitespace-only diff.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
